FEATURE: carousel-verification
DATE: 2026-10-02
SCOPE: verify the Carousel module, fix what is broken, and document it

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository). Consumers in the workspace (Apps/vGet, Apps/myinvitees/
app.myinvitees.com) mount vUX through a symlink and pick the changes up on the next page load;
neither currently imports vUX-carousel.js or vUX-touchHandler.js, so nothing in them changes.

Consumer-visible surface:
  - vUX-carousel.js        internals rewritten around a single slide index; public API unchanged.
                           start() before initialize() now throws; dot buttons lose their
                           id="b1".. attributes; config now applies live.
  - vUX-touchHandler.js    swipe crash fixed; touchHandler.css now linked.
  - assets/css/touchHandler.css  adds touch-action.
  - assets/css/carousel.css      unchanged, but now actually loaded.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION METHOD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No test runner exists, so the module was driven in headless Chromium (Playwright) over a test
page served from the repository root, asserting slide/dot/position agreement, computed styles,
listener behaviour and thrown messages. The same suite was run against the original files.

Baseline (original code):   13 passed, 14 failed
After the fixes:            28 passed, 0 failed  (one touch-CSS check added after the baseline)
Example page suite:         30 passed, 0 failed  (desktop and 375px phone)

The harnesses live in the session scratchpad, not the repository. Not verified: real touch input
on a physical device; the touch-action fix follows from the Pointer Events spec.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 1. Dots invisible and unclickable by default: carousel.css never linked (0px tall).
 2. Autoplay desync after a dot click or swipe: the screen, active slide and active dot drifted apart.
 3. Two carousels on a page moved each other's active dot (document-wide lookups).
 4. Viewport without an id: no slides found, no dots built ("#null> div").
 5. Swipe/drag threw on every gesture: TouchHandler wrote to an undeclared `viewport`
    (window.viewport, a non-element, in Chrome).
 6. speed = 0 stopped autoplay after one move (no transitionend for 0ms).
 7. Carousel hidden mid-slide stopped autoplay for good (transitioncancel not handled).
 8. Hover/press over a moving slide marked it finished early (mouseenter forced completed = 1).
 9. buttonStyle: only the first carousel's applied, it restyled every carousel, and carousel.css
    overrode it; errors were message fragments; an empty array was accepted.
10. container.onclick/onmouseenter/onmouseleave clobbered the consumer's handlers.
11. Config changes after initialize()/start() had no effect.
12. start() before initialize() threw on every tick.
13. No touch-action on the swipe area, so phones would hijack swipes as page pans; grab cursor never shown.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN LIMITATIONS (documented, not changed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 - Layout CSS (positioned container/viewport/slides) is the consumer's; see doc/carousel.md.
 - TouchHandler drags container.children[0], so the viewport must be the container's first child.
 - touchResponse decides at initialize() whether a TouchHandler exists; turning it on later is a no-op.
 - No slide-change callback; the example watches data-activeDisplay with a MutationObserver.
 - Dots are <div>s with no keyboard or ARIA support.
